Lab 16: Automating Identity Management
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

• Create Ansible playbooks to automate user and group creation in Identity Management (IdM) • Configure Host-Based Access Control (HBAC) and sudo rules using Ansible automation • Automate IdM server setup and client enrollment processes • Understand best practices for IdM automation and configuration management • Implement scalable identity management solutions using open-source tools

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

• Basic understanding of Linux system administration • Familiarity with YAML syntax and Ansible fundamentals • Knowledge of Identity Management concepts (users, groups, authentication) • Experience with command-line interface operations • Understanding of SSH key-based authentication • Basic networking concepts (DNS, LDAP)

Lab Environment
Ready-to-Use Cloud Machines: Al Nafi provides pre-configured Linux-based cloud machines for this lab. Simply click Start Lab to access your environment - no need to build your own virtual machines or configure complex networking.

Your lab environment includes: • idm-server: CentOS Stream 9 server for IdM installation • idm-client1: CentOS Stream 9 client for enrollment testing • ansible-control: CentOS Stream 9 with Ansible pre-installed

Task 1: Create a Playbook to Automate User and Group Creation
Subtask 1.1: Set Up Ansible Environment
First, we'll prepare our Ansible control node and install necessary collections.

Connect to the Ansible control node:
ssh student@ansible-control
Install required Ansible collections:
ansible-galaxy collection install freeipa.ansible_freeipa
ansible-galaxy collection install community.general
Create the project directory structure:
mkdir -p ~/idm-automation/{playbooks,inventory,group_vars,host_vars}
cd ~/idm-automation
Create the inventory file:
cat > inventory/hosts.yml << 'EOF'
all:
  children:
    idm_servers:
      hosts:
        idm-server:
          ansible_host: 192.168.1.10
          ansible_user: root
    idm_clients:
      hosts:
        idm-client1:
          ansible_host: 192.168.1.11
          ansible_user: root
    ansible_control:
      hosts:
        localhost:
          ansible_connection: local
EOF
Subtask 1.2: Create User and Group Management Playbook
Create the main playbook for user and group management:
cat > playbooks/manage-users-groups.yml << 'EOF'
---
- name: Manage IdM Users and Groups
  hosts: localhost
  gather_facts: false
  vars:
    ipaadmin_password: "RedHat123!"
    ipaserver_hostname: "idm-server.example.com"
    
    # Define groups to create
    idm_groups:
      - name: developers
        description: "Development team members"
      - name: sysadmins
        description: "System administrators"
      - name: managers
        description: "Management team"
    
    # Define users to create
    idm_users:
      - name: jdoe
        first: John
        last: Doe
        email: jdoe@example.com
        password: "TempPass123!"
        groups:
          - developers
      - name: asmith
        first: Alice
        last: Smith
        email: asmith@example.com
        password: "TempPass123!"
        groups:
          - sysadmins
          - developers
      - name: bwilson
        first: Bob
        last: Wilson
        email: bwilson@example.com
        password: "TempPass123!"
        groups:
          - managers

  tasks:
    - name: Ensure IdM groups exist
      freeipa.ansible_freeipa.ipagroup:
        ipaadmin_password: "{{ ipaadmin_password }}"
        name: "{{ item.name }}"
        description: "{{ item.description }}"
        state: present
      loop: "{{ idm_groups }}"
      delegate_to: idm-server

    - name: Ensure IdM users exist
      freeipa.ansible_freeipa.ipauser:
        ipaadmin_password: "{{ ipaadmin_password }}"
        name: "{{ item.name }}"
        first: "{{ item.first }}"
        last: "{{ item.last }}"
        email: "{{ item.email }}"
        password: "{{ item.password }}"
        update_password: on_create
        state: present
      loop: "{{ idm_users }}"
      delegate_to: idm-server

    - name: Add users to groups
      freeipa.ansible_freeipa.ipagroup:
        ipaadmin_password: "{{ ipaadmin_password }}"
        name: "{{ group_item }}"
        user: "{{ item.name }}"
        action: member
        state: present
      loop: "{{ idm_users }}"
      loop_control:
        loop_var: item
      with_subelements:
        - "{{ idm_users }}"
        - groups
      loop_control:
        loop_var: group_item
      delegate_to: idm-server
      vars:
        group_item: "{{ item.1 }}"
EOF
